+/**
+ * Select the explicit/implicit 1D shape value without materialising a local
+ * shape-factor array.  The reduced-shape branch mirrors the upstream call
+ * `Compute_shifted_shape_factor<1>(array + offset, x, i_new + offset)`.
+ * Its local write is at `offset + 1 + (i(x) - (i_new + offset)) + n`,
+ * which algebraically reduces to the absolute slot
+ * `1 + (i(x) - i_new) + n`.  Passing the high-order base and the absolute
+ * slot therefore preserves the shifted-pointer placement, including the
+ * in-bounds order-1 stencil that appears as a local shift of -2.  The regular
+ * branch uses the order-N shape at its original slot, so cell crossings retain
+ * the shifted old-shape prefix rather than the same-cell-only shape pair.
